    introHeading: "What is Physical Therapy?",
    intro: ["Physical therapy is a rehabilitation discipline focused on improving how the body moves and functions. Through guided exercise, hands-on techniques, movement retraining, and education, therapists address limitations in strength, mobility, coordination, balance, and endurance that make daily life harder.","It can help people of many ages and backgrounds: those recovering from a stroke or brain injury, adults managing balance concerns, people healing from surgery or orthopedic injury, and those living with long-standing pain or conditions that affect movement. For neurological conditions, therapy often emphasizes repetition, task-specific practice, and gradual challenge to support the nervous system in relearning movement patterns.","Exercise-based rehabilitation is widely supported by clinical research as a way to improve function, reduce pain, and lower fall risk. Results vary by person and condition, which is why careful assessment and a plan tailored to you are central to good care."],
    signsHeading: "Signs physical therapy may help",
