    introHeading: "What is Occupational Therapy?",
    intro: ["Occupational therapy is a health profession focused on helping people take part in the activities of everyday life. In this context, \"occupation\" means any meaningful task: getting dressed, cooking a meal, managing medications, using a computer, caring for family or returning to work.","In neurological rehabilitation, occupational therapy addresses the ways that brain injury, stroke, and other conditions can affect movement, sensation, thinking and energy. A therapist looks at the whole picture, including physical ability, cognitive skills, emotional well-being and the demands of your home and work environment, then designs activities that rebuild skills or offer workable alternatives.","Occupational therapy is widely used in rehabilitation settings, and approaches such as task-specific training, cognitive strategy training and environmental adaptation have research support in neurological recovery. Because every person's goals differ, therapy is tailored rather than one-size-fits-all. Patients in Southfield and nearby communities seek this care to regain confidence and safety at home and beyond."],
