    introHeading: "What is Speech and Language Pathology?",
    intro: ["Speech and language pathology, often called speech therapy, is the discipline concerned with how people understand and use language, produce speech, and use thinking skills such as attention and memory to communicate. A speech-language pathologist evaluates these abilities and designs therapy to rebuild them or to find practical workarounds.", "After a brain injury, communication can change in many ways. Some people have trouble finding words or following a conversation. Others speak clearly but struggle to organize their thoughts, stay on topic or read social cues. These cognitive-communication difficulties are common after traumatic brain injury and can affect relationships, work and independence.", "Speech and language pathologists have been part of Irvine's team since 1994, working alongside physical and occupational therapists, nursing and counseling. Because Irvine offers residential, apartment and outpatient programs, practice can carry over into the conversations and routines of daily life."],
